  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 10,
    "tagline": "Week 10 News · Nuclear Scores · Division Carnage · Four Weeks Left",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 10",
    "headline": "THE SITH WENT NUCLEAR. BARTON SCORED 151.66 AND STILL GOT BURIED.",
    "deck": "Week 10 turned the scoring dial until it snapped: Simpson Sith hung 160.94, Barton answered with 151.66 and still lost, Medford stayed molten at 144.98, and the playoff races got meaner with only four regular-season weeks left.",
    "story": [
      "Week 10 did not produce a Game of the Week. It produced a crime scene. Simpson Sith detonated for 160.94 against THE Barton Spartans, and Matt somehow answered with 151.66 and still walked away 2-8. That is 312.60 combined points in one matchup. Our older ESPN history export does not contain weekly box scores, so we cannot honestly crown it the all-time combined-score record from that archive. What we can say with certainty is that Simpson's 160.94 is the highest team score captured in the detailed 2026 weekly archive, topping Ticklesh!ts' 156.32 from Week 4, while Barton's 151.66 becomes the highest-scoring loss in that same archive.",
      "The funniest part is that the fireworks were not isolated. Medford MountainMen dropped 144.98 on Space Cadets and has now scored 112.30, 121.00, 110.98 and 144.98 over four straight weeks. Doug was 1-6 after Week 7. He is 4-6 now, and the Mountain has gone from punch line to avalanche. The 125.65 three-week scoring average is the hottest current stretch in the league.",
      "The Central still belongs to Turbulent Ticklesh!ts, and Tyler made sure nobody forgot it. A 131.24-83.22 demolition of Sullco pushed Ticklesh!ts to 7-3 with 1,164.00 points and a 72-38 all-play record, both league bests. The standings finally look more like the underlying numbers: this is not just a good record anymore. This is the league's heaviest offense dragging a division lead behind it.",
      "Out West, the crown changed hands. California beat Redwood 112.86-90.32 and moved alone to 8-2. Tavis has now banked eight wins despite sitting only fifth in total scoring and seventh in all-play, which makes California the league's great contradiction: maybe not the biggest hammer, but apparently the guy who keeps showing up when the nails are exposed. Redwood, once 7-1, has lost two straight and suddenly has company everywhere.",
      "And then there are the teams nobody wants to see despite their records. Off Boys reached 5-5 by flattening Eskimo Brothers 102.90-69.12 and owns a top-four scoring/all-play profile. Flint is only 3-7 but sits sixth in PF and fifth in all-play. Those are not comfortable bottom-half opponents. They are land mines with losing records painted on top."
    ],
    "awards": [
      {
        "emoji": "☢️",
        "title": "Nuclear Option",
        "team": "Simpson Sith",
        "detail": "160.94 points, the new high-water mark of the detailed 2026 archive. Danny did not merely win; he forced Week 10 into the record book."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "💀",
        "title": "Best Loss Nobody Wants",
        "team": "THE Barton Spartans",
        "detail": "151.66 points would have beaten every other team in Week 10 except Simpson. Instead it becomes the highest-scoring loss captured in the 2026 detailed archive."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🏔️",
        "title": "Avalanche Warning",
        "team": "Medford MountainMen",
        "detail": "144.98 points and four straight weeks above 110. Doug has gone from 1-6 to 4-6 while turning the Mountain into the hottest scoring stretch in the league."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🐯",
        "title": "Central Apex Predator",
        "team": "Turbulent Ticklesh!ts",
        "detail": "131.24 points, a 48.02-point beating of Sullco, and league-best marks in both PF and all-play. Tyler is done asking the standings for respect."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "👑",
        "title": "The Wild West Has a New Sheriff",
        "team": "California Un-Named Team",
        "detail": "112.86-90.32 over Redwood sends Tavis to 8-2 and gives California sole possession of the West lead."
      }
    ],
    "tidbits": [
      "Simpson's 160.94 is 4.62 points above Ticklesh!ts' previous 2026 high of 156.32. One huge Sunday was enough to rewrite the detailed-season ceiling.",
      "Simpson + Barton combined for 312.60. The historical ESPN export is season-level and does not include old weekly box scores, so calling that an all-time GFL record would be fake precision. For 2026 detailed history, though, it is the benchmark now.",
      "Barton scored 151.66 and took a loss. That is 29.70 points higher than the previous 2026 high-scoring loss, Barton's own 121.96 from Week 5. When bad luck finds Matt, apparently it brings a flamethrower.",
